DESCRIPTION:Sesame Street Day marks November 10\, 1969\, the day Sesame Str
 eet began regular broadcast through the National Educational Television sy
 stem. The show was not entertainment with lessons slipped in: it grew out 
 of a 1966 feasibility study commissioned by the Carnegie Corporation\, its
  stated target audience was inner-city disadvantaged children aged three t
 o five\, and the U.S. Office of Education agreed to cover half its budget.
  The anniversary is thoroughly documented\; the observance built on it is 
 not.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/sesame-street-day/
